From 4838b061f80758cea8601f66eca6466efe98c27f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes-agent-workflow contributor <noreply@hermes-agent-workflow>
Date: Sat, 25 Apr 2026 10:13:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] whatsapp: add react_to_message tool + adapter method
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds an emoji-reaction path so the agent can ack low-stakes group
messages without breaking flow with a [bot] text reply.

- gateway/platforms/whatsapp.py: WhatsAppAdapter.react_to_message()
  POSTs to the bridge /react endpoint with the WAMessageKey fields
  (chatId, messageId, fromMe, participant). Pass empty-string emoji
  to clear an existing reaction.
- tools/react_to_message_tool.py: new agent-callable tool with the
  same signature, registered under toolset='messaging'. Auto-discovered
  by tools/registry.py's AST scan. Gated on WhatsApp being configured
  and a session/gateway being active.

NOTE: the agent must know the messageId of the target message. That
metadata is in event.raw_message but not currently surfaced into the
prompt body — until that's plumbed, the agent can only react to
messages whose ids it has retained from earlier tool output (e.g. its
own prior reply's message_id). Follow-up: surface inbound messageId
to the prompt body in groups, similar to the existing
'[Display Name]' prefix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
